        "category": "offensive",
        "description": {
            "value": "<p><em>The Art of the Libra Twin Swords &mdash; Rozan J&#363;jiken.</em></p><p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per turn</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> You are wielding both @UUID[Compendium.isaacs-hb-pf2e.saint-class-features.Item.Libra Twin Sword (Right)] and @UUID[Compendium.isaacs-hb-pf2e.saint-class-features.Item.Libra Twin Sword (Left)]</p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> You hit the same creature with both Twin Swords this turn</p><hr /><p>The cuts cross. The target takes <strong>persistent bleed equal to your weapons' number of damage dice in d6s</strong> &mdash; 2d6 once you have striking, 5d6 at <em>Athena's Temper</em> &mdash; and is <strong>off-guard until the end of your next turn</strong>.</p><p><strong>Greater (8th level)</strong> The Twin Swords also gain <strong>deadly d8</strong>.</p><p><strong>Perfect (14th level)</strong> The deadly die becomes <strong>d10</strong>, the bleed dice become <strong>d8s</strong>, and a creature bleeding from The Crossing receives only <strong>half the Hit Points</strong> from any healing.</p><hr /><p>Granted by @UUID[Compendium.isaacs-hb-pf2e.saint-class-features.Item.Libra — the Weapons]. Target the creature you hit twice, then use this; the bleed, the off-guard and the halved healing are all applied for you.</p>"
        },
